298 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Atomicity ensures that a transaction is treated as a single unit of work, either all or none of the changes are applied. Consistency ensures that a transaction brings the database from one valid state to another. Isolation ensures that concurrent transactions do not interfere with each other. Durability ensures that once a transaction is committed, its changes are permanent and survive system failures.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
